# Aussie EcoGuard project instructions

- This repository implements the FIT3184 assignment. Read README.md and the
  relevant deployment documentation before changing a component.
- The current authorized scope is local cloud access and Agent Toolkit setup.
  Further project deployment is paused until the user requests it. Do not restart
  the student Learner Lab or run tutorial deployment examples as part of setup.
- The additional out-of-pocket budget is A$0. Do not enable billable cloud
  resources, start stopped servers, or upgrade account billing plans unless the
  user explicitly changes this constraint. Existing course credit and verified
  existing cloud allowances are the only authorized funding sources.
- Use the named ecoguard-personal profile for this personal-account Toolkit
  installation. Its default region is ap-southeast-2; Toolkit catalog and MCP
  endpoint use us-east-1. Keep the student default profile separate. Verify the
  selected profile, account, and operation region before cloud actions.
- Keep existing Terraform infrastructure in infra/aws and infra/gcp. Prefer
  changes to those definitions rather than rewriting the deployment in another
  framework. Oracle deployment templates target an existing server.
- Keep login caches, keys, tokens, .env files, and Terraform state outside Git.
  Do not print secret values or copy them into documentation or tool output.
- Distinguish local checks, real cloud connectivity, and full assignment
  acceptance. A successful identity query or MCP initialization alone does not
  establish deployment or complete the assignment.

